{"content":[{"c":["BEAM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Weaver’s beam—round wooden roller on which the cloth or carpet was wound during the weaving process in Bible times. The spears of the giant Goliath (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.17.7","r":"1Sam.17.7","rawR":"1Sam.17.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.17.7","value":"1Sam.17.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 17:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.19","r":"2Sam.21.19","rawR":"2Sam.21.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.19","value":"2Sam.21.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 21:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.20.5","r":"1Chr.20.5","rawR":"1Chr.20.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.20.5","value":"1Chr.20.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 20:5"},") and an Egyptian killed by Benaiah, one of David’s mighty men (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.23","r":"1Chr.11.23","rawR":"1Chr.11.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.23","value":"1Chr.11.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:23"},"), were compared to a weaver’s beam."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Tree trunk or log that has been squared and used for building purposes. King Solomon used beams and planks of cedar to build the temple (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.6.9","r":"1Kgs.6.9","rawR":"1Kgs.6.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.6.9","value":"1Kgs.6.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 6:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.3.7","r":"2Chr.3.7","rawR":"2Chr.3.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.3.7","value":"2Chr.3.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 3:7"},") and his “House of the Forest of Lebanon” (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.7.2,12","r":"1Kgs.7.2,12","rawR":"1Kgs.7.2,12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.7.2,12","value":"1Kgs.7.2,12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 7:2, 12"},"). Another mention of cedar beams probably refers to their aroma (",{"href":"?bref=Song.1.17","r":"Song.1.17","rawR":"Song.1.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.1.17","value":"Song.1.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Sg 1:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Crossbeam of a Hebrew balance from which the scales were hung by cords."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Beam (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") or log (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") referred to by Jesus (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.7.3-5","r":"Matt.7.3-5","rawR":"Matt.7.3-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.7.3-5","value":"Matt.7.3-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 7:3-5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.6.41-42","r":"Luke.6.41-42","rawR":"Luke.6.41-42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.6.41-42","value":"Luke.6.41-42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 6:41-42"},"). Jesus contrasted the beam in an accuser’s eye with the mote (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") or speck (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") in his brother’s eye."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Beam","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 17:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.17.7","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.17.7","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.17.7"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 21:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.19","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.19","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 20:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.20.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.20.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.20.5"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.23","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.23","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.23"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 6:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.6.9","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.6.9","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.6.9"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 3:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.3.7","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.3.7","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.3.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 7:2, 12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.7.2,12","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.7.2,12","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.7.2,12"},{"anchorText":"Sg 1:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.1.17","rawQueryValue":"Song.1.17","sourceRefExact":"Song.1.17"},{"anchorText":"Mt 7:3-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.7.3-5","rawQueryValue":"Matt.7.3-5","sourceRefExact":"Matt.7.3-5"},{"anchorText":"Lk 6:41-42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.6.41-42","rawQueryValue":"Luke.6.41-42","sourceRefExact":"Luke.6.41-42"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"00ecab53a9342e06429855c75aa912a2108e4ffa23170e6f73761f1f855e5613","sourceItemName":"Beam","sourceItemOrder":118,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Beam","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Beam","title":"Beam","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}